    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_32c4fe5e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes images of three political figures (Bernie Sanders, Elizabeth Warren, and Cory Booker) with the repeated phrase 'free stuff!' in a sarcastic and mocking tone. The text 'las cosas mas gratis' (the most free stuff) is presented as if it were a quote from the debate, implying that the politicians are promoting or emphasizing free stuff as a key policy. The meme's intent is to ridicule the politicians by suggesting they are obsessed with or overly focused on 'free stuff,' which is presented as a trivial or unserious policy focus. This is a form of political satire that may be perceived as dismissive or condescending toward the candidates' policy positions. While it does not contain explicit hate speech or targeted abuse against specific protected groups, it does use a mocking tone that could be seen as harmful to the political discourse by reducing complex policy debates to a simplistic and potentially misleading caricature. The meme's overall intent is to entertain through ridicule while potentially undermining the seriousness of the candidates' policy discussions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3c078a44"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
